            {
              "title": "Hatcher, Algebraic Topology, proof of Poincare duality and local coefficients, Chapters 3.3 and 3.H",
              "url": "https://pi.math.cornell.edu/~hatcher/AT/AT.pdf"
            }
          ]
        },
        "statement": "Let $X$ be a Hausdorff manifold, $X=U\\cup V$ an open cover, and $\\mathcal L$ a local system of abelian groups. There is a natural exact sequence\n$$\\cdots\\to H_c^p(U\\cap V;\\mathcal L)\\to H_c^p(U;\\mathcal L)\\oplus H_c^p(V;\\mathcal L)\\to H_c^p(X;\\mathcal L)\\to H_c^{p+1}(U\\cap V;\\mathcal L)\\to\\cdots.$$\nThe maps into the union are extension maps obtained by excision. If $X$ is oriented of dimension $n$, cap with its compatible integral compact-support orientation classes compares this sequence with homology Mayer–Vietoris in degrees $n-p$. The ladder commutes when the homology connecting map leaving degree $n-p$ is multiplied by $(-1)^{p+1}$. No choice principle is assumed. All maps respect a coefficient-ring action commuting with the local transports.",
        "proof_strategy": "direct",
        "dependency_level": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "lem-choice-free-local-coefficient-duality-on-a-coordinate-ball",
