        "statement": "Let $B$ be an oriented coordinate ball of dimension $n\\ge0$ and let $\\mathcal L$ be a local system of abelian groups on $B$. Cap with the integral support orientation classes gives isomorphisms\n$$H_c^k(B;\\mathcal L)\\xrightarrow{\\sim}H_{n-k}(B;\\mathcal L)$$\nin every integer degree. Under a coordinate contraction trivialization with fiber $A$, both sides are $A$ for $k=n$ and zero otherwise, and the displayed nonzero map is the identity on $A$. No choice principle is assumed; any commuting coefficient-ring action is respected.",
