        "statement": "Let $R$ be an associative unital ring with $1\\ne0$ and no zero divisors, embedded as a unital subring in a division ring $K$, let $N=K/R$ as a right $R$-module, and let $C_*$ be a chain complex of right $R$-modules with $C_0,C_1$ finite free and $C_j=0$ for $j<0$. If either $H_0(C_*)=0$ or every right ideal of $R$ is principal, then restriction to cycles induces an isomorphism of abelian groups\n$$\\kappa:H^1(\\operatorname{Hom}_R(C_*,N))\\longrightarrow\\operatorname{Hom}_R(H_1(C_*),N).$$\nIf the coefficient Hom groups carry a compatible commuting left action, this is an isomorphism for that action as well. No choice principle is assumed.",
