          "def-chain-complex-with-coefficients-by-tensoring",
          "def-homology-object-of-a-chain-complex",
          "def-opposite-ring"
        ],
        "justified_by": [],
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "ai-altered",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "Tim D. Cochran, Kent E. Orr, and Peter Teichner, Knot concordance, Whitney towers and L²-signatures, Remark 2.6",
              "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/math/9908117"
            },
            {
              "title": "Charles A. Weibel, An Introduction to Homological Algebra, Chapter 3",
              "url": "https://math.mit.edu/~hrm/palestine/weibel/03-tor_and_ext.pdf"
            }
          ]
        },
        "statement": "Let $R$ be a unital ring with $1\\ne0$ and no zero divisors. Suppose both Ore conditions hold: any two nonzero elements have a nonzero common right multiple and a nonzero common left multiple. Let $R\\subseteq K$ be a unital embedding into a division ring such that every element of $K$ is a right fraction $as^{-1}$ with $a\\in R$ and $0\\ne s\\in R$.\n\nFor every right $R$-module $M$, the right $K$-module $M\\otimes_RK$ is represented by fractions $[m,s]$ with $m\\in M$ and $0\\ne s\\in R$, corresponding to $m\\otimes s^{-1}$. The equality criterion is\n$$[m,s]=[n,t]\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\text{there exist }0\\ne u,v\\in R\\text{ with }su=tv\\text{ and }mu=nv.$$\nIn particular, $[m,s]=0$ if and only if $ma=0$ for some $0\\ne a\\in R$. Thus the kernel of $M\\to M\\otimes_RK$, $m\\mapsto m\\otimes1$, is exactly the set of elements with a nonzero right annihilator, and $M\\otimes_RK=0$ if and only if every element of $M$ has a nonzero right annihilator.\n\nThe functor $-\\otimes_RK$ is exact on arbitrary right $R$-modules, so $K$ is flat as a left $R$-module. For every chain complex $C_\\bullet$ of right $R$-modules, the canonical map gives a natural isomorphism\n$$H_i(C_\\bullet)\\otimes_RK\\xrightarrow{\\ \\cong\\ }H_i(C_\\bullet\\otimes_RK)$$\nfor every integer $i$. No finite-generation, finite-presentation or boundedness assumption on the modules or complexes is required.\n\nThe corresponding left-module assertions also hold: $K$ is flat as a right $R$-module, $1\\otimes m$ is zero in $K\\otimes_RM$ precisely when $am=0$ for some $0\\ne a\\in R$, and $K\\otimes_R-$ commutes with the homology of arbitrary left-module chain complexes. All assertions require no choice axiom.",
        "proof_strategy": "direct",
        "dependency_level": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "lem-torsion-free-abelian-extensions-preserve-group-ring-domains",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "title": "Nonsplit torsion-free abelian extensions preserve absence of group-ring zero divisors",
        "deps": [
